  "output": "Here's the full performance analysis of the HR Policy Bot codebase. I found **12 significant issues** across the backend and frontend:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis — HR Policy Bot\n\n### Critical Issues\n\n#### 1. N+1 Database Connections (`src/api/routes.py:121-187`)\nEvery API endpoint creates a fresh `DatabaseManager()` instance instead of reusing one. Under concurrent load, SQLite's write lock serializes all requests.\n\n```python\n# BEFORE — new connection per request\nasync def list_queries(...):\n    db = DatabaseManager()  # new connection every time\n    ...\n\n# FIX — singleton at module level\n_db: DatabaseManager | None = None\n\ndef get_db() -> DatabaseManager:\n    global _db\n    if _db is None:\n        _db = DatabaseManager()\n    return _db\n```\n\n#### 2. Unclosed DB Connections / Memory Leak (`src/data/db.py`)\nEvery method opens `aiosqlite.connect()` as a one-shot call. Under high concurrency this can exhaust file descriptors. Add a persistent connection with explicit close in the FastAPI shutdown hook.\n\n---\n\n### High Severity\n\n#### 3. Event Listener Accumulation (`static/js/app.js:391-417`)\n`showFeedbackControls()` wires new click listeners on every query response without removing old ones. After 10 queries, 10 copies of each listener fire per click.\n\n```javascript\n// FIX — clone node to strip old listeners before re-wiring\nconst oldBtn = document.getElementById('submitFeedback');\nconst newBtn = oldBtn.cloneNode(true);\noldBtn.replaceWith(newBtn);\nnewBtn.addEventListener('click', submitFeedback);\n```\n\n#### 4. JSON Parsed Per Row in Bulk Queries (`src/data/db.py:136-146`)\n`list_queries()` calls `json.loads()` for every row in a loop — O(n) repeated parsing. Pre-parse all rows in a batch comprehension, or normalize `agents_invoked` into a join table.\n\n---\n\n### Medium Severity\n\n#### 5. Unbounded Domain Semaphore Dict (`src/fetch/engine.py:42-47`)\n`_domain_semaphores` uses `defaultdict` and grows indefinitely. Use `cachetools.TTLCache(maxsize=500, ttl=3600)` to evict stale entries.\n\n#### 6. Unclosed `httpx.AsyncClient` on SIGKILL (`src/fetch/engine.py:49-59`)\nThe HTTP client leaks if the shutdown hook doesn't fire. Register an `atexit` handler as a safety net alongside the existing `shutdown_event`.\n\n#### 7. DOM Query Repeated Per Click (`static/js/app.js:391-401`)\nFeedback button handlers re-query all buttons on every click. Cache references in a `const buttons = Array.from(...)` and use event delegation on the parent instead.\n\n#### 8. WebSocket Reconnection Thundering Herd (`static/js/app.js:90-92`)\nFixed 3-second reconnect fires for all clients simultaneously on server restart. Add exponential backoff with jitter:\n\n```javascript\nlet delay = 1000;\nws.onclose = () => {\n    const jitter = Math.random() * 0.2 * delay;\n    setTimeout(connectWebSocket, delay + jitter);\n    delay = Math.min(delay * 1.5 + Math.random() * 1000, 30000);\n};\nws.onopen = () => { delay = 1000; };  // reset on success\n```\n\n#### 9. O(n²) Citation String Wrapping (`static/js/app.js:482-493`)\n`wrapWithCitations()` compiles a new `RegExp` and runs `replace()` over the full response text for each citation. With 8 agents × 4 instruments = 32 passes over a 10KB response. Pre-build a term→marker map and do a single-pass token scan instead.\n\n#### 10. Duplicate Specialist Metadata (`specialist.py:23-56` vs `api/routes.py:18-59`)\n`_SPECIALIST_METADATA` and `_AGENT_CONFIG` contain the same data. Extract to a shared module and import from one source of truth.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| # | Issue | Severity | File | Lines |\n|---|-------|----------|------|-------|\n| 1 | N+1 DB connections | Critical | routes.py | 121-187 |\n| 2 | Unclosed DB connections | Critical | db.py | all methods |\n| 3 | JS event listener leak | High | app.js | 391-417 |\n| 4 | JSON parsed per row in loop | High | db.py | 136-146 |\n| 5 | DB init race condition | High | main.py | 58-66 |\n| 6 | Unbounded domain semaphore dict | Medium | engine.py | 42-47 |\n| 7 | Unclosed HTTP client on SIGKILL | Medium | engine.py | 49-164 |\n| 8 | DOM re-query per click | Medium | app.js | 391-401 |\n| 9 | WS reconnection thundering herd | Medium | app.js | 90-92 |\n| 10 | O(n²) citation string wrapping | Medium | app.js | 482-493 |\n| 11 | Duplicate specialist metadata | Medium | specialist.py/routes.py | 23-59 |\n| 12 | Citation dedup inefficiency | Low | orchestrator.py | 203-223 |\n\nThe two most impactful fixes are **#1** (DB connection reuse) and **#3** (JS listener cleanup) — both are simple changes with immediate, measurable effect. Want me to implement any of these?\n",
